Subject: [PATCH] PCI: qcom: wait qcom,ep-latency after PERST# deassert (bring-up)

The downstream MSM PCIe driver waits qcom,ep-latency milliseconds after
releasing PERST# before starting link training; the SM-T825 stock DT
sets 10 ms for the QCA6174 on RC0. Honour the property if present.
Bring-up patch: the property is not in the mainline binding.

--- a/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/controller/dwc/pcie-qcom.c
@@ -307,9 +307,20 @@
 
 static void qcom_ep_reset_deassert(struct qcom_pcie *pcie)
 {
+	u32 ep_latency_ms = 0;
+
 	/* Ensure that PERST has been asserted for at least 100 ms */
 	msleep(PCIE_T_PVPERL_MS);
 	qcom_perst_assert(pcie, false);
+
+	/*
+	 * Downstream qcom,ep-latency: time the endpoint needs after PERST#
+	 * before link training. Without it the SM-T825 QCA6174 left the LTSSM
+	 * in Polling.Compliance.
+	 */
+	of_property_read_u32(pcie->pci->dev->of_node, "qcom,ep-latency", &ep_latency_ms);
+	if (ep_latency_ms)
+		msleep(ep_latency_ms);
 }
 
 static int qcom_pcie_start_link(struct dw_pcie *pci)
